# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VR Realms Creator Kit — .gitignore
# The repo holds DOCS + the lean UE project (Config + Content).
# Build caches and the 162 MB Tools/ binaries do NOT go in git —
# the WorkshopTool ships as a ZIP attached to a GitHub Release.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- UE build caches / generated (never commit) ---
VRRealms/Intermediate/
VRRealms/Saved/
VRRealms/DerivedDataCache/
VRRealms/Build/
VRRealms/Binaries/
VRRealms/.vs/
VRRealms/*.sln

# --- Shipped tool binaries (distributed via GitHub Releases, not git) ---
# ⚠ `Tools/*` WITH THE STAR, NOT `Tools/`. Git never descends into a directory
#   excluded by name, so a later `!Tools/*.ps1` would be silently ignored and the
#   VRR Creator scripts would never be committed — a fresh clone would have no
#   updater at all. Excluding the CONTENTS instead leaves the directory visible,
#   which is what makes the negation below work.
Tools/*
!Tools/*.ps1

# --- Build output of Tools\New-KitRelease.ps1 (uploaded to a Release, not git) ---
_release/

# --- WorkshopTool runtime/user state (must never ship) ---
**/workshop_tool_settings.json
**/CookTemp/
**/Staging/
*.pdb

# --- Internal dev notes — NEVER ship to creators (mention internal assets/process) ---
CLAUDE.md
KIT_BUILD_NOTES.md
KIT_TEMPLATES_SETUP.md
GAME-SIDE_SETUP.txt
KitInternal/
*_DEV_NOTES*
*_INTERNAL*
*GAME-SIDE*

# --- Author-machine launcher shortcut (ships inside the ZIP, never in git — abs paths) ---
*.lnk

# --- Dev-only material generator (materials ship as baked .uassets; creators need zero setup) ---
CreateAvatarBasicMaterial.py

# --- OS / editor junk ---
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*~
